    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Playing Flooded Strand (which can only fetch Plains or Island) means the player cannot produce black mana this turn to cast Fatal Push on Ocelot Pride. This gives the opponent a free attack with Ocelot Pride (gaining life via lifelink) and a token at end step, letting the board spiral out of control.",
      "action_taken": "Played Flooded Strand as their land for the turn",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp (or Marsh Flats, cracking for Swamp) to have {B} available, then cast Fatal Push targeting Ocelot Pride immediately, preventing token generation.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 9,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 7,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Fetched Godless Shrine and paid 2 life to enter untapped for black mana, but they had a Swamp already in hand that could provide black mana for Thoughtseize this turn. The 2 life paid for the shockland was unnecessary.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Godless Shrine (entering untapped, paying 2 life) off Flooded Strand to cast Thoughtseize.",
      "better_line": "Fetch Hallowed Fountain (entering tapped, saving 2 life) or a surveil land like Undercity Sewers/Meticulous Archive for card selection, then play Swamp from hand untapped to cast Thoughtseize. This saves 2 life while providing better color diversity (W/U/B) across the two lands.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 11,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 10,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Ocelot Pride on the board (a 1/1 creature), Fatal Push would cleanly destroy it for just 1 mana, and the opponent already has revolt enabled (no permanents left the battlefield, but Fatal Push doesn't need revolt for a 1-mana creature). Casting Thoughtseize costs 2 life (putting Valley at 15) and only takes a card from hand, while the Ocelot Pride on the battlefield continues to threaten token generation at end of turn. Fatal Push removes the immediate board threat efficiently. Thoughtseize is better when you need information or to strip a key card before the opponent can cast it, but the Ocelot Pride is already deployed and will generate value if it survives to the end step. That said, Thoughtseize does provide information and can strip a follow-up threat, and Valley still has Orcish Bowmasters available to flash in during the end step to potentially deal with token generation, so this is close but slightly suboptimal.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Thoughtseize targeting the opponent",
      "better_line": "Cast Fatal Push targeting Ocelot Pride to remove the token-generating threat immediately, preserving life total and preventing end-step triggers. Thoughtseize could be cast next turn after seeing what the opponent draws.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 12,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 11,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Fetched a second Godless Shrine and paid 2 life (going from 13 to 11) when a basic Swamp would have entered untapped for free and provided the same mana to cast Orcish Bowmasters. Against an aggressive Ocelot Pride deck, 2 life is meaningful.",
