      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Swamp instead of Flooded Strand is slightly suboptimal. Flooded Strand as a fetch land enables Revolt for Fatal Push, which is highly relevant since the opponent has Ocelot Pride on board (1/1 that will generate tokens). With two Fatal Pushes in hand and the opponent's Ocelot Pride being a critical threat that needs answering, having a fetch land on the battlefield ready to sacrifice for Revolt gives much more flexibility. The Swamp just provides black mana which is already available from two Godless Shrines. Playing the fetch land now keeps open the option to crack it on the opponent's turn to enable Revolt-powered Fatal Push to kill larger threats (up to MV 4) if needed, while still providing mana access.",
