      "description": "Playing Plains instead of Flooded Strand is slightly suboptimal. Flooded Strand provides deck thinning and, more importantly, can enable Revolt for Fatal Push (relevant if drawn later or in future turns). Additionally, fetching with Flooded Strand puts a land in the graveyard, which helps fuel Phlage's escape cost if the player ever needs to use graveyard resources. The player already has cards in the graveyard including Fatal Push copies, so having a fetch land available on the battlefield to crack at instant speed for Revolt is more valuable than saving 1 life. With the opponent at 20 and the player at 11, the 1 life matters somewhat, but the tactical flexibility of a fetch land on board outweighs this.",
