      "player": "MiMo Sarge",
      "decision_index": 97,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "MiMo Sarge has exactly enough mana (RRWW from 5 lands) and enough cards in graveyard (7 other cards, need 5) to escape Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury. The opponent is at 10 life with no creatures on board. Phlage would enter as a 6/6, deal 3 damage (opponent to 7), gain 3 life, and threaten another 3 damage on attack next turn. This is a game-dominating play that was completely passed on.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to cast either Seasoned Pyromancer or Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury from the graveyard.",
      "better_line": "Escape Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury by paying RRWW and exiling 5 cards from graveyard. This puts a 6/6 on an empty board, deals 3 to opponent (bringing them to 7), and gains 3 life - likely winning the game in short order.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 83,
      "player": "MiMo Sarge",
      "decision_index": 100,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury can be escaped here for {R}{R}{W}{W} exiling 5 cards from the 7 available in graveyard. It creates a 6/6 body, deals 3 damage to the opponent (putting them to 7), and gains 3 life. This is vastly superior to Seasoned Pyromancer's graveyard ability which only creates two 1/1 tokens. Phlage threatens lethal next attack (6 combat + 3 trigger = 9 vs opponent's 10, nearly lethal) and applies enormous pressure.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to activate Seasoned Pyromancer from graveyard to create two 1/1 Elemental tokens",
      "better_line": "Escape Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury to create a 6/6 threat that deals 3 damage and gains 3 life on entry, putting massive pressure on the opponent at 10 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 84,
      "player": "MiMo Sarge",
      "decision_index": 100,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With the opponent at 7 life, Phlage escape was available (RRWW + exile 5 cards from 8-card graveyard) for a 6/6 that deals 3 damage on entry (putting opponent to 4) and gains 3 life. Playing Elegant Parlor (tapped land) as the first action is suboptimal sequencing - if they plan to cast Phlage this turn, they should lead with Phlage to avoid revealing information. If they don't cast Phlage at all, it's a much bigger mistake. Additionally, Arid Mesa would have been a better land drop as it can fetch an untapped land.",
      "action_taken": "Played Elegant Parlor (enters tapped) as their first action",
      "better_line": "Cast Phlage via escape immediately (RRWW from Mountain + Arena of Glory + 2x Sacred Foundry, exiling 5 graveyard cards) to deal 3 damage to opponent (putting them to 4 life) and deploy a 6/6 threat, then play a land.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 98,
      "player": "MiMo Sarge",
      "decision_index": 116,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 7 life, played Watery Grave paying 2 life (going to 5) before casting Thoughtseize. They already have B mana available from Swamp/Godless Shrine to cast Thoughtseize this turn. Should cast Thoughtseize first to see opponent's hand and gather information before committing to a land drop. Additionally, paying 2 life for Watery Grave to enter untapped is likely unnecessary since they already have 6 lands with all colors available - it could safely enter tapped.",
      "action_taken": "Played Watery Grave paying 2 life (untapped) before casting any spells",
      "better_line": "Cast Thoughtseize first using existing B mana to see opponent's hand, then play Watery Grave tapped (saving 2 life at a precarious 7 life total)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 106,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 127,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 5 life, casting Thoughtseize loses 2 life going to 3, which puts them in range of Phlage's escape (3 damage ETB) that the opponent has available with 9 cards in graveyard and sufficient mana. The life loss is very dangerous in this position.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Thoughtseize, going from 5 to 3 life",
      "better_line": "Hardcast Solitude (3WW) to deploy a 3/2 lifelink creature that can block and gain life, helping stabilize at the critically low 5 life total. Solitude's lifelink is far more valuable than the disruption from Thoughtseize when the self-damage puts you in lethal range of Phlage escape.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 106,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 127,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 5 life with Phlage in opponent's graveyard (which deals exactly 3 on ETB), paying 2 life for Thoughtseize drops to 3 life - exactly in Phlage escape lethal range. The opponent has enough mana colors (2x Sacred Foundry, Mountain, Arena of Glory, Plains) and 9 cards in graveyard (needs 5 to exile) to potentially escape Phlage next turn for exactly lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Thoughtseize, going from 5 to 3 life",
      "better_line": "Cast Solitude as a 3/2 lifelink creature (have 7 lands including white sources for 3WW). The lifelink body provides both a clock and life buffer. Even without a creature to exile with ETB, a 3/2 lifelink is critical when at 5 life facing potential Phlage escape.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 107,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 129,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Casting Thoughtseize at 5 life drops Gem25F Valley to 3 life, which puts them in lethal range of Phlage's escape (3 damage ETB trigger). The opponent has Phlage in graveyard with 9 cards available to exile 5, and enough mana ({R}{R}{W}{W}) across their lands. At 5 life, Phlage's 3 damage is survivable; at 3 life it's lethal. The only nonland card taken (Voice of Victory, a 1/3) is not worth the risk.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Thoughtseize at 5 life, taking Voice of Victory and dropping to 3 life",
      "better_line": "Don't cast Thoughtseize. Hold Solitude and Fatal Push as interaction, stay at 5 life to survive Phlage's ETB trigger if it escapes. Voice of Victory (1/3 with mobilize) is not threatening enough to justify the 2 life cost in this position.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 108,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 133,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 3 life and Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury can be escaped from the graveyard for {R}{R}{W}{W} + exile 5 cards. MiMo Sarge has 9 cards in graveyard (enough to exile 5) and the mana to pay {R}{R}{W}{W} (Mountain, Arena of Glory for {R}{R}, Plains and Sacred Foundry/Elegant Parlor for {W}{W}). Phlage's ETB deals 3 damage to any target, which is exactly lethal against the opponent at 3 life.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Voice of Victory for 2 mana instead of escaping Phlage for the kill.",
      "better_line": "Escape Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury from the graveyard, targeting the opponent with the 3 damage ETB trigger for lethal.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 112,
      "player": "MiMo Sarge",
      "decision_index": 137,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 3 life. MiMo Sarge has Phlage in the graveyard with escape cost {R}{R}{W}{W} + exile 5 cards (9 other cards available in graveyard). With Sacred Foundry entering untapped (pay 2 life), the 4 untapped lands (Arena of Glory, existing Sacred Foundry, existing Elegant Parlor, new Sacred Foundry) would produce exactly {R}{R}{W}{W} to escape Phlage. Phlage's ETB deals 3 damage to any target, which is exactly lethal against the opponent at 3 life. Instead, Elegant Parlor enters tapped, leaving only 3 untapped lands and making Phlage uncastable this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Elegant Parlor (enters tapped) off Arid Mesa",
      "better_line": "Fetch Sacred Foundry (pay 2 life, enters untapped), then escape Phlage for {R}{R}{W}{W} exiling 5 graveyard cards, dealing 3 damage to opponent at 3 life for lethal",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 116,
      "player": "MiMo Sarge",
      "decision_index": 142,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 3 life facing lethal on board (Voice of Victory + Ragavan = 5+ damage next attack), spending 1 life to fetch a land with 8 lands already in play is wasteful. Voice of Victory is MV 2, so Fatal Push already kills it without needing revolt. The life point matters significantly at 3 life.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Flooded Strand to fetch a land, paying 1 life to go to 2 life with 8 lands already on board.",
      "better_line": "Cast Fatal Push targeting Voice of Victory immediately (MV 2, no revolt needed), preserving the life point and eliminating the most dangerous threat that also locks out spells during opponent's turn. Then hardcast Solitude next turn to exile Ragavan and gain a lifelink blocker.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 120,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 146,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 3 life facing Ragavan (2/1) and Voice of Victory (1/3 with Mobilize 2), only removing one threat leaves the player still facing lethal or near-lethal damage next turn. Both creatures need to be addressed this turn since Voice of Victory prevents casting during opponent's turn.",
      "action_taken": "Likely cast only Fatal Push, leaving Ragavan on board while at 3 life",
      "better_line": "Cast Fatal Push targeting Voice of Victory AND hard-cast Solitude (5 mana available from 8 lands) targeting Ragavan to completely clear the board and survive. Solitude's lifelink body also provides a blocker and life buffer.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 120,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 146,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem25F Valley is at 3 life facing lethal next turn from Ragavan (2/1) + Voice of Victory (1/3 with Mobilize 2 creating two 1/1 attackers) = 5 damage. Voice of Victory also prevents casting spells during opponent's turn, so they can't Fatal Push during MiMo's combat. They have the mana to hard-cast Solitude (3WW with 7+ untapped lands) to exile Voice of Victory, which would remove the spell-lock, the mobilize tokens, and leave Solitude as a 3/2 lifelink blocker against Ragavan.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting anything, leaving lethal attackers on board with no ability to interact during opponent's turn due to Voice of Victory's spell-lock.",
      "better_line": "Hard-cast Solitude (3WW) targeting Voice of Victory to exile it, removing the combat lock and lethal threat. Solitude's 3/2 lifelink body can then block Ragavan, and Fatal Push remains available for future use.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 121,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 150,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Voice of Victory prevents opponents from casting spells during MiMo Sarge's turn. At 3 life, Gem25F Valley faces lethal from Ragavan (2/1) + Voice of Victory (1/3) + two Mobilize warrior tokens. By passing without removing Voice of Victory or Ragavan, Gem25F Valley will be completely locked out of casting Solitude or Fatal Push during MiMo Sarge's next combat, making lethal unavoidable.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting any spells during their own combat step.",
      "better_line": "Cast Solitude (evoking by exiling Fatal Push) to exile Voice of Victory, removing both the spell-lock and a significant attacker. Alternatively, at minimum cast Fatal Push on Ragavan to reduce incoming damage, since these spells cannot be cast during the opponent's turn while Voice of Victory is in play.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 122,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 152,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Voice of Victory prevents casting spells during opponent's turn, and the opponent has lethal on board next attack (Voice of Victory 1 + Mobilize 2 warriors + Ragavan 2 = 5 damage vs 3 life). By passing without removing threats, Gem25F Valley will die next turn with no ability to interact.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting any spells, holding Fatal Push and Solitude for a 'better moment'",
      "better_line": "Hard-cast Solitude (3WW, which is available from 8 lands including multiple white sources) targeting Voice of Victory to exile it, removing both the lethal Mobilize threat and the 'can't cast spells during opponent's turn' restriction. Alternatively, Fatal Push Voice of Victory (MV 2) to at least reduce incoming damage significantly.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 122,
      "player": "Gem25F Valley",
      "decision_index": 152,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Opponent is at 3 life and MiMo Sarge has no cards in hand except a land. Activating Seasoned Pyromancer from the graveyard for {3}{R}{R} would create two 1/1 Elemental tokens, providing additional attackers to close out the game next turn against an opponent at 3 life. With 6 untapped lands and nothing else to spend mana on, there's no reason not to activate this.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to activate Seasoned Pyromancer's graveyard ability, leaving 6 mana unused with no other plays available.",
      "better_line": "Activate Seasoned Pyromancer's graveyard ability ({3}{R}{R}) to create two 1/1 Elemental tokens, increasing board pressure against an opponent at 3 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 126,
      "player": "MiMo Sarge",
      "decision_index": 164,
    }
  ],
